WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
The headline finding is robustness without a cost
to clean accuracy.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.880
On the original, unshifted test sets,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.860
color equivariant ResNets perform on par with
vanilla ResNets.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.840
But when the test images are hue-shifted, the gap
opens dramatically.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.820
On Flowers-102,

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.800
average accuracy across hue shifts jumps from about
thirteen percent for the baseline

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.780
to thirty-three percent for the fully equivariant model,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.760
and similar gains appear on CIFAR-100 and Stanford Cars.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.740
In the controlled long-tailed experiment the
equivariant network reaches ninety-one percent

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.720
against the baseline's seventy-two percent,

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.700
with the biggest improvements exactly on the rare
classes that shape sharing is meant to help.
